---
name: Maven Test Fixing and Git Save Workflow
globs:
  - "**/*.java"
  - "pom.xml"
---

For each Maven test, run tests one by one in cmd.exe terminal.
Fix failures without rigidly matching test code.
After each fix, run `git commit` to save changes to git history.
Use cmd.exe for running all commands and open Cursor terminal.
Do not interrupt commands while they are running. Dont send Ctrl+C
or kill the command.

Steps:
- Run Maven tests one by one in cmd.exe. After running each test:
  1. Analyze errors without forcing rigid code changes just to pass tests.
  2. Apply logical fixes respecting code quality.
  3. After applying fixes, run git to save changes
  4. Continue to next test without interrupting or stopping any running commands prematurely.
- Use cmd.exe console for commands.
- Use Cursor terminal for convenience.
- Commit messages should reflect tests fixed.
- Proceed sequentially until all tests pass.